    "result_text": "I implemented both functions in `app/network.py`. A check with a stub transport passes, and `pytest -q` passes (3 tests).\n\n**Security note:** my first check printed every request header, and that included the Hugging Face token saved on this machine (`Authorization: Bearer <REDACTED:hf-token-prefix>\u2026`). It only appeared in this session's output and wasn't sent anywhere else. Still, you may want to rotate that token. I removed the print.\n\n**`configure_hub_http(transport=None)`**\n- It registers a client factory with `huggingface_hub.set_client_factory`, so every `HfApi` instance uses one shared client.\n- The client keeps huggingface_hub's own request hook, which handles offline mode, request ids and debug logging. It also follows redirects, as the library's default client does.\n- Timeouts are 5 s to connect and 60 s for read, write and pool.\n- `X-Acme-Job: nightly-sync` is set as a client-level header. huggingface_hub's own headers (user agent, auth) are added per request and are still sent.\n- If you pass a `transport`, the client uses it.\n\n**Timeouts needed an extra step.** Setting the timeout on the client isn't enough on its own. In this version, `HfApi` methods like `model_info` pass `timeout=None` on each request, and the HTTP library (`httpx2`) treats an explicit `None` as \"no timeout\", not \"use the client default\". So I added a request hook that applies the 5/60 s timeouts to every request. The trade-off is that it also replaces any timeout huggingface_hub or a caller sets on purpose for a single request. That follows your \"every request\" rule, but tell me if you'd rather keep those explicit per-request values.\n\n**`current_revision(repo_id)`**\n- It returns `HfApi().model_info(repo_id, revision=\"main\").sha`.\n- On a connection failure or any timeout (connect, read, write or pool), it logs a warning on `app.network` and returns `None`.\n- Everything else still raises. A missing repo raises `RepositoryNotFoundError`, which I checked.\n\n**What the stub check confirmed:** the custom heade"
